	(text "R16 (10 KΩ, pull-up) — holds PULSE_IN at a solid 3.3 V \nwhile the reed switch inside the tipping bucket is open. \nWithout this, the input pin would float and pick up random noise; \ninstead, a \"no tip\" state is a clean, defined HIGH, \nand a tip is a clean, defined LOW.\nR37 (10 KΩ) + C52 (1 µF) — RC low-pass filter \nevery mechanical reed switch bounces for roughly a millisecond \nwhen it closes, producing several rapid make/break transitions \ninstead of one clean edge. \nThis RC stage smooths that bounce into a single slow, monotonic \ntransition, so downstream logic doesn't see it as several separate tips.\nU9 (SN74LVC1G17, Schmitt trigger) — a plain comparator would still flicker \non a slow, noisy ramp near its switching threshold. \nThe Schmitt trigger's two-threshold hysteresis means the ramp has to \ncross a high threshold to register HIGH and a distinctly lower threshold to \nregister LOW again — so it outputs exactly one sharp, unambiguous logic edge per \nphysical tip, on the PULSE_MCU line into the microcontroller.\nD4 (VESD05A1-02V-G3-08, TVS diode) — rain gauges live outdoors at the end of a \nlong cable, which acts as an antenna for ESD and lightning-induced transients. \nD4 clamps those surges before they can reach the Schmitt trigger or the MCU pin."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 188.468 366.522 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "a40581fb-243b-4cbf-911f-fa76fd139a5f")
	)
	(text "5VDC"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 525.78 171.45 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.032 2.032)
				(thickness 0.4064)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "a8b04ffd-5b98-4f5b-8bea-4dc306070033")
	)
	(text "RTC [WITH BACKUP BATTERY]"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 379.222 213.614 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3 3)
				(thickness 0.4)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "be7d4493-0686-435c-a3e9-cfef9ecd1563")
	)
	(text "Q1 is configured as a level shifter for the receive path, \nconverting the SDI-12 bus level to the MCU's RX input. \nThe SDI-12 bus itself is driven by the buffer (U6), \nwhich controls both the HIGH and LOW states of the bus."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 16.51 345.948 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "ccde21ea-0436-4229-9383-c1ead9d5c688")
	)
	(text "INPUT PROTECTION (F1 / Q3 / DZ2):\nF1 (PTC resettable fuse) is placed in series with VIN, upstream of Q3\n(DMP3098L reverse-polarity MOSFET) and DZ2 (BZX84-C15 zener clamp).\nDuring an overcurrent or surge event, DZ2 clamps the voltage; F1 limits\nand interrupts the current through that clamp path, then self-resets\nonce the fault clears - protecting Q3, DZ2, and downstream traces/\ncopper from sustained high current. No GDT is fitted upstream - this\nstage is sized for overcurrent faults, ESD, and moderate transients,\nnot high-energy lightning-induced surges."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 230.886 124.968 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.032 2.032)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "e99608e4-cc08-42e8-aa9c-314f639b15a3")
	)
	(text "MCU PROG"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 37.592 36.576 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3 3)
				(thickness 0.4)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "ea148901-6b49-44c6-a949-ebf16340db4a")
	)
	(text "SDI-12 to UART"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 33.528 279.654 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3 3)
				(thickness 0.4)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "ebca36f1-dfd9-4dd3-8b0d-f763a6b80618")
	)
	(text "Not for low-level \nAC inputs"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 209.042 331.216 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
		)
		(uuid "f0e8ceac-761c-44d8-9672-4c8a915b59a2")
	)
	(text "Max Tx Radiated Power: +14 dBm\nRx Sensitivity: -125 dBm\nPower Supply: From 1.8V to 3.6V\nPower Consumption:\nTx: 27 mA\nRx: 5 mA\nIdle: 1.8 μA\nEmbedded Software\nMemory Size for Client Firmware: 57Kb\nSDK: Yes\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 24.13 222.758 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "f5bb6edb-93a8-4fd6-b521-47ad924fcaa9")
	)
